  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Documentation of Newly Discovered Angkorian Sites on Kulen Mountain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phnom Kulen is a culturally important mountain range near Angkor Archaeological Park. About 30 archeological sites and many more lesser-known and unidentified sites ranging in date from the 8th to the 12th century are endangered by subsistence farming and looting in the area. This project includes site mapping, assessment, and a heritage protection education and outreach program.</narrative>
  </description>
